sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-girardia-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The octanol-induced head-shape change in G. dorotocephala is instructive rather than a toxic or housekeeping defect, because it yields one of several coherent, ecologically valid morphologies rather than regeneration failure or disorganized growth, with no intermediate morphologies observed.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Coherent discrete head shapes show the octanol effect is instructive rather than toxic";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Emmons-Bell M, Durant F, Hammelman J, Bessonov N, Volpert V, Morokuma J, Pinet K, Adams DS, Pietak A, Lobo D, Levin M, “Gap Junctional Blockade Stochastically Induces Different Species-Specific Head Anatomies in Genetically Wild-Type Girardia dorotocephala Flatworms”, International journal of molecular sciences (2015), doi:10.3390/ijms161126065; section “3. Discussion › 3.1. Perturbation of Bioelectric Networks Produces Inter-Species Morphological Change”. Scope: Octanol-treated G. dorotocephala regenerates"
}
