    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms161126065>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "The head morphology alteration effect was instructive, and not merely one of toxicity or a house-keeping defect, because the outcome was not merely disruption of regenerative ability or a generalized mis-patterning (e.g., tumor or other disorganized growth), but rather resulted in one of several coherent (and ecologically-valid) morphologies.".
